From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 19:47:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rpcrt4: Enable idle cleanup without a FIXME.

Wine keeps idle connections pooled until their association is released,
which costs the open connection only; Windows 11 returns RPC_S_OK
(tools/startupgapsprobe misc).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/dlls/rpcrt4/rpc_server.c b/dlls/rpcrt4/rpc_server.c
index ddc5ca7f3e7..75c28d9ea95 100644
--- a/dlls/rpcrt4/rpc_server.c
+++ b/dlls/rpcrt4/rpc_server.c
@@ -1615,7 +1615,9 @@ RPC_STATUS WINAPI RpcMgmtStopServerListening ( RPC_BINDING_HANDLE Binding )
  */
 RPC_STATUS WINAPI RpcMgmtEnableIdleCleanup(void)
 {
-    FIXME("(): stub\n");
+    /* Windows then closes client connections that have been idle for a while; ours stay pooled until the
+     * association they belong to is released, which costs nothing but the open connection */
+    TRACE("()\n");
     return RPC_S_OK;
 }
 
